{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788809575336082001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"bumpy-slight-bobwhite","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"f20e7be7c8cedb49bc9c75668435d223e4c495548efa03962661eec5595c7a3c","event_uuid":"57daa844-78e9-489e-a32e-002e1f2af4b0","position":{"commit_sha":"b1b5f7c127458e16c74aaf5436bd334a53405ee9","position":"1788805725351500070-57daa844-78e9-489e-a32e-002e1f2af4b0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"6eb9162cd594d1a75add88d3b6cf8e94fee5b1285716b46862c6368947d04eae","event_uuid":"26df9d51-d8ee-4f66-83d9-82ba22d5b625","position":{"commit_sha":"14b3746e3486065cde1645e2c5bd49481fe89347","position":"1788805738776222608-26df9d51-d8ee-4f66-83d9-82ba22d5b625"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"4d0c0df1eb6982ecd3bcfe368f82ab11cae85c625d298b3d05bf66d093917463","event_uuid":"8a7d38e4-0a86-4fe7-8f2d-56a546cd4981","position":{"commit_sha":"6ab763f5d2a546f403d4f9329e619d0918848163","position":"1788805741704689243-8a7d38e4-0a86-4fe7-8f2d-56a546cd4981"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788805725351500070,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"26df9d51-d8ee-4f66-83d9-82ba22d5b625","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"bafa-2a33-6136-4fc5"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`docs/llm-framework.md` \"Extras taxonomy\" (`:43-68`) lists two extras and never mentions `evals`; no document tells a client project how to run plan-replay, fixture-mining, or provider-parity against its own `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` and `.rebar/evals/`. 71 open, parentless `fixture-drift:` tasks (for example `00b4-b253-3052-4181`) were filed by hand for story 67aa's acceptance criterion from `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/fixtures/drift-report.md`, each `discovered_from` the closed epic `65dd-e93b-666a-4caa`; `git grep fixture-drift` on origin/main is empty, and `src/rebar/llm/evals/fixture_mining/heal.py`'s only ticket producer is `_file_unreliable_ticket` (`heal.py:83` `UNRELIABLE_TITLE_PREFIX = \"unreliable-criterion: \"`, `:359-364`), while drift goes to `.rebar/fixture_heal_drift.md` (`:462`). Those 71 tasks have no producer and no consumer. Cites are on origin/main 2e81cb9767c1.\n\n## Approach\nAdd a `docs/llm-framework.md` section titled \"Running the eval harnesses against your own criteria\" after \"Usage log\" (`:509-593`), stating: install with `pip install 'nava-rebar[agents,evals]'`; criteria live in `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` and project prompts in `.rebar/prompts/<id>.md` (override order `src/rebar/llm/evals/fixture_selection.py:71-99`); specs in `.rebar/evals/<prompt_id>.eval.yaml` win over packaged ones (`src/rebar/llm/evals/eval.py:58-75`); set `[llm.evals] corpus_root` (default `.rebar/evals`); then the exact commands: `rebar prompt eval <prompt_id>`; `rebar criteria eval [<criterion_id>] --changed-since origin/main --require-live`; `rebar criteria heal --dry-run` then `rebar criteria heal` (cap `$25`, `src/rebar/_cli/_llm_eval_commands.py:136`; outputs `.rebar/fixture_heal_drift.md`, `.rebar/fixture_heal_ledger.jsonl`, emitted `.rebar/evals/*.eval.yaml`; files `unreliable-criterion: <id>` tickets); `python -m rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay tier0 --candidate current`, `tier1 --n 20`, `tier2 --criteria E1` (writes under `<corpus_root>/plan-review-gate/replay/`, `--store name=path` for another store, `--ledger` to relocate spend); `python -m rebar.llm.evals.provider_parity --slot standard --epochs 3` (writes `<corpus_root>/provider-parity/provider_parity_results.json`); `REBAR_LLM_EVALS_CORPUS_ROOT=/scratch/evals` for CI. Add an `[evals]` bullet to the taxonomy and the `llm.evals.corpus_root` row to \"Configuration\" (`:408`). Add a `docs/llm-example-configs.md` snippet with `[llm.evals]` and `corpus_root = \".rebar/evals\"`. Disposition of the 71 tasks, through the MCP server: for each id returned by `search(\"title:fixture-drift: status:open\")`, `transition_ticket(id, \"open\", \"closed\", close_class=\"obsolete\", reason=\"superseded by the scheduled fixture-heal loop (rebar criteria heal, heal.py), which re-mines every criterion on fixture_heal.interval_days, records drift in .rebar/fixture_heal_drift.md, and files one unreliable-criterion: ticket per criterion that fails three consecutive re-mines; per-entry drift tickets have no producer and no consumer\")`; `obsolete` is reason-required administrative vocabulary that mints a disposition verdict without an LLM run (`docs/ticket-model.md:125-145`, `src/rebar/_commands/gates.py:143-148`); then `comment_ticket(\"65dd-e93b-666a-4caa\", ...)` recording the batch. Release note (non-breaking, contract section): eval harness roots are configured (`llm.evals.corpus_root`, default `.rebar/evals`); `rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay.ledger.DEFAULT_LEDGER_PATH` removed (ledger defaults resolve at call time); `provider_parity --out` defaults under the corpus root; the `evals` extra is registered.\n\n## Scope\n`docs/llm-framework.md`; `docs/llm-example-configs.md`; `docs/release-notes.md`; `tests/unit/test_llm_framework_docs.py` (new: asserts the section heading and each command string); tracker writes on the 71 tickets plus one comment. No source files.\n\n## Testing\nHappy: `pytest tests/unit/test_llm_framework_docs.py -q`; `python scripts/check_docs_index.py`; every command in the section executed once in a temp client repo (`rebar init`, copy `.rebar/criteria_routing.json`) with `--dry-run` where offered; `rebar search \"fixture-drift:\" -o json | jq '[.[]|select(.status==\"open\")]|length'` prints `0`. Edge: `rebar prompt eval nonexistent-id` reports the missing spec path (`.rebar/evals/nonexistent-id.eval.yaml`) rather than a traceback; re-running the disposition batch is a no-op (each ticket is already closed, so the optimistic-concurrency refusal, exit 10, is expected and skipped).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The section is present with the seven command lines verbatim (doc test passes).\n- [ ] `[evals]` appears in the extras taxonomy and `llm.evals.corpus_root` is documented with its default and env name.\n- [ ] 0 open `fixture-drift:` tickets remain; each closed record carries `close_class: obsolete` and the reason (`rebar show <id> -o json`).\n- [ ] The release-notes entry is present.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/llm-framework.md","reason":"client section; taxonomy; config row"},{"path":"docs/llm-example-configs.md","reason":"[llm.evals] snippet"},{"path":"docs/release-notes.md","reason":"contract entry"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_llm_framework_docs.py","reason":"new doc test"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","bafa-2a33-6136-4fc5"],["parent","e47b-d3ef-338f-4bcd"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"e47b-d3ef-338f-4bcd","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_id":"741b-b0da-0098-45d8","ticket_type":"story","title":"Document running the eval harnesses against a client's own criteria; register the evals extra; close the 71 orphaned fixture-drift tasks","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["57daa844-78e9-489e-a32e-002e1f2af4b0","26df9d51-d8ee-4f66-83d9-82ba22d5b625","8a7d38e4-0a86-4fe7-8f2d-56a546cd4981"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788809575336082001,"uuid":"98c0824c-611b-491e-a448-5316e426a546"}